 you just  cease to exist but after defeating the  man god thor dispatches loki's entire  army which had basically had no trouble  destroying asgard up to that point and  thor does this without any real  difficulty now after allowing certain to  invade asgard thor makes his way to the  tapestry of fate which basically  contains the threats that make up  reality itself intending to destroy it  so the cycle of ragnarok will be broken  but despite pleas from those who sit  above in shadow not to do so thor  basically destroys the tapestry with one  swing of his hammer and with it also  destroys the life tree idracil and those  who sit above in shadow so this version  of thor was basically able to take out a  group of gods who they themselves were  god's two gods so we know he's powerful  and also because he quite literally  destroyed reality but is he more  powerful than superboy prime well  superboy prime technically debuted in dc  comics presents number 87 in 1985 by  elliott magnan and kurt swann who by the  way i don't know how many guys know this  kurt swann drew superman for like 35  years he's like the superman artist to  give you guys perspective like kurt swan  art that is kind of like unfinished art  or like the art he drew for comic book  panels where it's like black and white  it shows the frame of the comic all that  kind of stuff that sells for tens if not  hundreds of thousands of dollars this  guy's art is on a whole different level  but superboy prime didn't actually adopt  his namesake until infinite crisis in  2006. he's basically kal-el from earth  prime which is really supposed to be  dc's version of our world where  superheroes only exist as fictional  characters and no one has superpowers  now kal-el is the last known survivor of  the planet krypton who's sent to earth  by his parents before the planet is  completely incinerated and he's found  and adopted by jerry and naomi kent who  give them the name clark now when clark  is 15 his powers mani